Evaluate the situation described. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {3, 6, -1, -4, -3, 1, 4, 6};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) acc += a[i];
return acc;

Examine the case described here. What does this string routine return?
String s = "doiiy";
int acc = 0, target = 'z';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

Figure out the requested quantity. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {-1, 3, 4, 8, 10, 11, 12, 15};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 21) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 21) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

The following case is given. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(10);
Node b = new Node(30);
Node c = new Node(15);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

A typical exam item asks this: Tracing this code:
int[] a = {5, 9, 11, 16, 19, 22, 25, 28, 33};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 9) return steps; if (a[mid] < 9) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

